      "sourceDuration": 16.44,
      "words": "Good morning. Welcome to Signal Market Watch. I'm Liza. A volatile start to the week: oil has pulled back, stocks are cautiously higher, and investors are bracing for major U.S. bank earnings and Wednesday's inflation report. We begin with what moved overnight.",
      "playbackSpeed": 1.04
    },
    {
      "id": "global_market",
      "kind": "voice",
      "showSceneId": "global_market",
      "start": 23.8,
      "duration": 17.133333333333333,
      "end": 40.93333333333333,
      "source": "r4/global_market.mp4",
      "role": "LASSE",
      "sourceDuration": 17.48,
      "words": "Asian shares were mixed on Monday, while U.S. stock-index futures edged higher. Reuters reported Brent crude near one hundred four dollars a barrel after retreating from recent highs. That is still an expensive energy backdrop, and markets remain sensitive to every new geopolitical headline.",
      "playbackSpeed": 1.02
