      "source": "r4/earnings.mp4",
      "role": "LIZA",
      "sourceDuration": 17.424,
      "words": "Now to Wall Street. Major U.S. banks begin third-quarter reporting this week. Analysts expect a strong earnings season, but the question is not simply profits. Investors will scrutinize credit losses, loan demand and management guidance for signs that higher costs are beginning to bite.",
      "playbackSpeed": 1.04
    },
    {
      "id": "recap",
      "kind": "voice",
      "showSceneId": "world_outlook",
      "start": 60.7,
      "duration": 18,
      "end": 78.7,
      "source": "r2/news_open.mp4",
      "role": "LIZA",
      "sourceDuration": 18.73,
      "words": "Markets are facing a real test this week. Bank earnings are about to arrive, inflation data are due Wednesday, and oil is still above one hundred dollars a barrel. Technology shares have powered expectations higher. But can those profits withstand expensive money? Lasse, what is the tension investors need to understand?",
      "playbackSpeed": 1.04
    },
    {
      "id": "midpoint",
      "kind": "graphics",
      "showSceneId": "earnings",
      "start": 78.7,
      "duration": 6,
      "end": 84.7,
