      "start": 107.4,
      "duration": 15.566666666666666,
      "end": 122.96666666666667,
      "source": "r2/oil.mp4",
      "role": "LIZA",
      "sourceDuration": 16.2,
      "words": "And now energy is complicating the picture. Brent crude has been above one hundred dollars, according to Monday's market reports. That can raise shipping and manufacturing costs. If profits look strong but households and businesses face higher bills, where do you look for the warning signs?",
      "playbackSpeed": 1.04
    },
    {
      "id": "inflation",
      "kind": "voice",
      "showSceneId": "inflation",
      "start": 122.96666666666667,
      "duration": 18.333333333333332,
      "end": 141.3,
      "source": "r2/cpi.mp4",
      "role": "LASSE",
      "sourceDuration": 18.704,
      "words": "Start with the major banks. Watch loan demand, credit losses, and what executives say about customers. Then Wednesday's consumer inflation report. A hotter reading could keep pressure on bond yields and highly valued shares. A cooler one could ease it. Neither outcome is certain. That's why this week matters.",
      "playbackSpeed": 1.02
    },
